Diamond package substrates are specialized thermal-management and packaging materials designed to transfer heat away from high-power electronic components. Synthetic diamond offers exceptionally high thermal conductivity, electrical insulation, and mechanical stability, making it suitable for applications where conventional materials struggle to maintain operating temperatures.

As semiconductor devices become more compact and powerful, effective heat dissipation is increasingly important for performance, reliability, and product lifespan. Diamond-based substrates and heat spreaders can help manage thermal loads in gallium nitride (GaN) radio-frequency devices, power electronics, optoelectronic systems, and high-performance computing equipment.

